1. Description of Fix:
- F7: Explicit capability gating inventory and audit.
  List each capability and what it actually gates. Gate what the kernel has now, and list the rest as gating nothing. Do not imply more (AGENTS.md rules 9 and 10).
- In `docs/architecture.md`:
  Added section "Capability Table & Enforcement Status (K4-R3 F7)" with an exhaustive inventory table documenting all 8 resources in the vocabulary:
  * `device:camera`: Gating nothing (no camera driver or MMIO mapping exists in kernel).
  * `device:microphone`: Gating nothing (no audio input driver or DMA buffer exists in kernel).
  * `device:audio`: Gating nothing (Intel HDA tone driver planned for K5c).
  * `fs:read`: Gating token request only (in-kernel FAT16/FAT32 readers exist; ring 3 user file descriptor read syscalls are deferred to K6-0).
  * `fs:write`: Gating nothing (kernel is strictly read-only; denied for all callers).
  * `compute:expression`: Gating nothing (mathd evaluator runs in user space).
  * `compute:verify`: Gating token request only (ring 0 package authentication in trust.rs uses cryptographic primitives; no ring 3 user compute syscall exists).
  * `reserved`: Gated permanently (refused by from_manifest; cannot be held by any user process).
- In `kernel/src/cap.rs`:
  Updated doc comments on `Resource` and added `pub(crate) fn gating_status(self) -> &'static str` and `pub(crate) fn has_live_kernel_subsystem(self) -> bool`.
- In `kernel/src/trustselftest.rs`:
  Added committed test auditing the capability table against live kernel subsystems (3 live: FsRead, ComputeVerify, Kernel; 5 unbuilt/gating nothing: Camera, Microphone, Audio, FsWrite, ComputeExpression).

